\begin_layout Standard
The controller is accessed by sending two-byte commands.
 The first byte specifies the command,
 and the second contains any required data.
 To send a command:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Wait until IN (00FDh) bit 1 is zero.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
OUT (01FCh),command_byte
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
OUT (00FCh),data_byte
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If the command returns data,
 then to read back the data,
 do:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Wait until IN (00FDh) bit 0 is 1.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Read data from IN (00FCh).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To read the status of the printer,
 do an IN (01FCh) twice in succession.
 If the values read don't match,
 repeat until they do.
 The bits in the byte returned are:
