\begin_layout Standard
The GSX driver (DDESP.PRL) checks for the presence of the light pen by reading port 0A7h and checking the result is not 0FFh.
 NEWSDESK does a slightly different check,
 enabling the screen (OUT 0xF8,
 0x07) and immediately checking that bits 6 and 7 of port 0A7h are zero.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 12-bit position counter remains unchanged until the pen sensor is activated.
 When it is activated,
 the counter starts decrementing,
 and continues to decrement until the next horizontal retrace.
 Thus the vertical position of the pen is detected by manually counting the number of horizontal retraces before it is triggered;
 the horizontal position by reading the position counter.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
An outline of the code in DDESP that reads the light pen position:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Wait for port 0FDh bit 6 to go high (ie,
 if the printer is doing anything,
 wait for it to finish).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Disable interrupts.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Wait for vertical retrace to go high (2 successive reads of port 0A7h have bit 6 set)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Save the initial 12-bit value of the position register.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Wait for vertical retrace to go low (2 successive reads of port 0A7h have bit 6 clear)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Wait for horizontal retrace (read of port 0A7h with bit 5 set,
 followed by read with bit 5 clear).
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
If vertical retrace is now high,
 finish.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
If current position value differs from previous value,
 the sensor has been triggered.
 Record X = (previous position - current position),
 Y = current Y coordinate.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Increment Y.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Repeat steps 6-9 for 288 screen lines,
 or until vertical retrace goes high.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Re-enable interrupts.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This may produce more than one pair of coordinates;
 if so,
 the light pen position is taken to be their average.
\end_layout

