\begin_layout Standard
The interface was supplied with a joystick driver DEFJOY.COM,
 which converted joystick movements into keypresses.
 This works by patching the running copy of CP/M to add code to the interrupt handler;
 every 16 interrupts,
 it checks the joystick position and injects the appropriate scancodes into the keyboard queue.
 Since DEFJOY.COM uses hardcoded addresses and memory areas within CP/M,
 it only works on PCW8000 CP/M with BIOS 1.4.
 
\end_layout

