\begin_layout Standard
On output,
 write 48h (ie,
 set the 8251 Break and Reset signals) to reset the card.
 Other bits should be 0.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
0A7h Data (read/write)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
On power-up,
 if there is no network connection,
 the card will send the byte sequence 00 90 99 00 to the PCW.
 This signifies 'ring broken at current station'.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A full description of the character sequences used to control the card,
 and the meanings of the bytes it returns,
 are outside the scope of this document.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
ASD Uninet
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This was announced by ASD in May 1987 as 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

an improved version of the Northern Computers Network system
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 which could allow a PCW to act as a server.
 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Northern Computers Network system
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 probably means Multilink,
 since the PCW Multilink card was made by Northern Computers.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Amstrel
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
HM Systems produced a version of their 
\noun on
Minstrel
\noun default
 server for Amstrad networking.
 This was an S-100 system running TurboDOS,
 which combined the features of MP/M and CP/Net.
 PCWs could thus either use it as a CP/Net fileserver,
 or behave as dumb terminals to 8-bit or 16-bit programs running on the server.
 It is likely that PCW workstations would have been connected to the server by RS232,
 rather than with specialised networking hardware.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Scanners / Image Capture
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
JOYCE does not emulate scanners or other image capture devices,
 so this section is sketchy at best.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
MasterScan
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The MasterScan is an optical sensor which clips to the print head of the PCW dot-matrix printer.
 The user is instructed to remove the printer ribbon,
 and the MasterScan software then programs the printer to draw a vertical line in graphics mode with minimal line spacing.
 As the head goes to and fro,
 the sensor is polled to scan the image.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The sensor is read from port 0DFh - the bottom bit is 0 for light,
 1 for dark.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The user guide for 'The Desktop Publisher' by Database Software mentions a 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Dart Scanner
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 which probably refers to the MasterScan,
 since it was sold by Dart Electronics.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
ProScan
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
ProScan is a package comprising a Naksha hand scanner,
 an interface to connect it to the PCW,
 and software to drive it.
 The software can also use an Amstrad FX9000T / FX9000AT fax machine as the image capture device.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The interface is accessed on ports 0E9h-0EFh.
 Ports 0EAh-0EDh appear to select what image capture device is to be used:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
0EAh Fax (FX1)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
0EBh Fax (FX2)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
0ECh Hand scanner
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
0EDh Unknown,
 but there is at least some support for it in the software;
 possibly a second type of hand scanner.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Digitisers
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Video capture devices were made by Electric Studio and Rombo.
 I don't have any software or drivers for these,
 so can't give any detail on how they operated.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
OCR input
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Issue 6 of 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

8000 Plus
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 describes the Oberon Omni-Reader,
 which scans printed text and supplies it to a computer.
 This uses RS232 rather than a dedicated interface,
 so on a PCW input from the Omni-Reader would come through the CPS8256 serial port.
\end_layout

