\begin_layout Subsection
While the link is running
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The server now waits for a packet from the client,
 and reacts depending on what it receives.
 The packet types used vary depending on LocoLink version.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
LocoLink v1.03 / v1.04
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The server supports the following packet types:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
14h Disconnects the link and shuts down.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
21h Check space for file.
 Packet contains a little-endian 32-bit value (file length),
 followed by the filename.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
2Eh Create file.
 Packet contains a little-endian 32-bit value (file length),
 followed by the ASCIIZ filename.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
3Bh Append data bytes to currently open file.
 Packet contains the bytes to append.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
48h Close file.
 Packet contains a word (probably file CRC).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
6Fh Create directory.
 Packet contains ASCIIZ path name.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
7Ch Find first file.
 Packet contains directory search flag (0 to search for directory,
 1 for file) followed by ASCIIZ filename.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
It returns the following packet types:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
55h Result.
 Two bytes follow.
 The first is the type of the packet it is replying to,
 the second is an error flag (0 if succeeded,
 other value if failed).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
62h Invalid packet type received.
 No bytes follow.
\end_layout

