\begin_layout Description
*2 LocoLink v2.x expects all pathnames to be absolute,
 eg Z:
\backslash
LETTERS
\backslash
PENNY.LS2.
 The client must also ensure that passed file names are in upper case,
 as the server does not check or enforce this.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
*3 The current directory set by function 3Bh is returned by function 47h but it does not affect operations in any other way since (as mentioned above) absolute paths need to be passed to all the other functions.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
*4 The search attribute is passed in AL whereas in the original INT 21h API it is passed in CX.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
*5 Unlike 'find first file',
 the result of 'find next file' is returned in the result packet rather than as a separate transfer.
 It consists of one word (AX) followed by bytes 0x12 onward of the find file data (but without the terminating zero byte on the filename;
 the caller has to deduce this using the packet length).
\end_layout

