\begin_layout Standard
Note that these packets may be larger than the equivalent packets sent by LocoLink v2.02.
 For example,
 function 0Eh (log in drive) now passes a drive number,
 since this version of LocoLink allows the host PC to switch between the PCW's drives.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
0CCh In response to a packet of type 0B9h.
 The packet contains the requested data.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The server may send the following packet types:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
18h Acknowledgement.
 Sent in response to a packet of type 05h,
 2Bh,
 0DFh or 0F2h.
 The first byte is the type of the packet it is acknowledging.
 For type 05h there are 1-20 For type 0F2h there is a second byte of data.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
2Bh Keep-Alive.
 The client acknowledges with a type 18h packet.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
93h End of DOS function call (success).
 Contains two bytes:
 the value returned by the function in AX.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
A6h End of DOS function call (failure).
 Contains two bytes:
 the DOS error code.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
0B9h Server requests data from client.
 Contains two bytes:
 the first byte is a code giving the source of the data,
 the second is the maximum data size.
 The client returns the data in a type 0CCh packet.
 The source codes are:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Description
11h Fixed length - copied from DX in original function call
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
36h Fixed length - copied from DTA
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
5Bh Fixed length - copied from SI in original function call
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
80h ASCIIZ (eg:
 filename) - copied from DX in original function call
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
0A5h ASCIIZ (eg:
 filename) - copied from SI in original function call
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
0CAh ASCIIZ (eg:
 filename) - copied from DI in original function call
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
0EFh Fixed length - copied from immediately after previous parameter
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Description
0DFh Data transfer from server to client.
 The first byte gives the destination of the data (using the same codes as 0B9h),
 the remainder of the packet is the data.
 Client acknowledges with a type 18h packet.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
0F2h Keep-alive?
 Appears to include one byte of data.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Version 3 of the LocoLink server on the PCW supports the same range of DOS function calls as version 2.
 However LocoLink for Windows and LocoLink 16 only use functions marked +.
 The other functions are present but may not be thoroughly debugged (for example,
 trying to get or set the volume label in LocoLink 3.00 always appears to fail with a 'drive not ready' error).
\end_layout

