\begin_layout Standard
Once a block is sent,
 the receiving system should verify the checksum and send 0 on its L line if OK,
 1 if error.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If there is an error the transfer is abandoned,
 and the transmitting system moves to the next file (if there is one).
 Otherwise the file is sent as a stream of bytes,
 followed by another End of Block sequence.
 Again,
 once all bytes have been sent the transmitting system reads input line L to determine if there was an error.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The transmitting system will then send either the header of the next file,
 or End of Transmission.
\end_layout

